  "needs": {
    "container": true,
    "reason": "The versions of jackson-annotations, jackson-databind and junit-jupiter are in no file of the project: they come from the imported jackson-bom 2.18.1 and junit-bom 5.11.3 published on Maven Central (checked: each pins its artifacts to its own version). Only the effective POM, which fetches those BOMs, states them. Whether shop-cli is built depends on the command line (-Dwith-cli)."
  },
  "traps": [
    "Module directories (model, service, cli) differ from artifactIds (shop-model, shop-service, shop-cli).",
    "shop-cli is a module only under the profile cli, activated by -Dwith-cli: the default reactor has two member modules (model, service), a reader that takes every pom.xml on disk finds three. build_tags records the profile that selects it; the aggregator at the root is the workspace root, not a member.",
    "junit-jupiter is declared once in the parent's dependencies and inherited by every child and by the pom-packaged parent itself; declared_in stays pom.xml.",
    "No child declares a version: guava and the sibling modules get theirs from the parent's dependencyManagement (guava.version, project.version), jackson and junit from the imported BOMs.",
    "The sibling modules (shop-model, shop-service) are written as coordinates in the child poms but are units of this project: they belong in depends_on, not dependencies.",
    "The BOM imports (jackson-bom, junit-bom, scope import) are not dependencies of any unit. The pluginManagement entries only fix the versions of plugins the default lifecycle runs in every module; they are listed once, under the parent, with scope build.",
    "The Java level differs per module: the parent sets maven.compiler.release 21, inherited by shop-parent, shop-service and shop-cli; model/pom.xml overrides it with 17 for shop-model. A reader that stops at the parent gives 21 everywhere.",
    "resolved for jackson-annotations, jackson-databind and junit-jupiter is read from jackson-bom 2.18.1 and junit-bom 5.11.3 as published on Maven Central at those versions; guava's comes from the parent's dependencyManagement.",
    "cli/pom.xml writes <version>${picocli.version}</version>; the value 4.7.6 is a property of the parent pom, so declared is 4.7.6 with declared_in pom.xml#properties.picocli.version, not the child file."
  ]
